	"descriptionMarkdown": "This is Destiny.\nStarship properties and utilities:\nSize: 93(w)x117(h)\nWeight: 882t\nCargo: 20x\nThrusters: 5x\nTanks: 100K\nEnergy: 13.3MW / 395MJ\nTurrets: 13x top,10x sides,6x rear-> 29x total + 3x top laser\n\nIt's self sustain and prevents any overloads of asteroid collectors.\nShip contains controller where fuel consumption can be set.\nShip contains indicator systems for levels of energy,fuel,water and ammo.\nShip contains blinking navigation lights.\nIn future it can be upgraded for nuclear power.\nOriginal design combined with proper functionality.\n\n© Designed by Velda\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@VeldaGames/\n\n\n\n\nThrusters control on this ship with explanation:\nOne tick counter combinator:\nInput - CLOCKS < 60. Input connected to output.\nOutput - CLOCKS and connected to second set-up combinator (read below).\n\nSecond set-up combinator:\nReads the tick counter output from the first combinator.\nOutput symbol = 1 is connected to both pumps which are pumping fuel into engines.\nDefault number on input: CLOCKS <=1\nOn the pumps is set condition: symbol = 1\n\nExplanation:\nIn Factorio, 1 second = 60 ticks.\nPumps have rate 1200/s and we have 2 pumps (2 types of fuel). 2400 divide 60 -> 1 tick = 40/s\nIf the ship has 5 engines with max. fuel usage 120/s each, that's 600/s total. So 1% is 6 fuel units per second. Max. engine efficiency starts at ~10%, so we need 60/s -> that's 1.5 ticks ->\nThus, you need to set-up number in second combinator to 1 for 10% efficiency.\n(3 would be 120/s and that would be ~20%, 6 would be 40%, etc.)",
